# [TLS](../wg/tls.html)

## Summary

The TLS Working Group met to discuss several active working group drafts and individual proposals. Key topics included updates and formal verification of Extended Key Update, codepoint registry management for Composite ML-DSA, secondary client authentication mechanisms, HTTP-level post-quantum pinning (PQ-HSTS), and integrating eXtendable-Output Functions (XOF) into the TLS 1.3 key schedule.

---

## Key Discussion Points

### Extended Key Update for TLS 1.3
- **Draft:** `draft-ietf-tls-extended-key-update`
- **Presenters:** Yaroslav Rosomakho, Nick, Felix Linker

- **Specification Updates:**
  - Updated terminology to replace "epoch" with "generation" to prevent collisions with DTLS epochs.
  - Exporters are now generation-aware; TLS must inform applications of the active EKU generation. Legacy exporter APIs remain supported for generation 0 for backward compatibility.
  - PSK session resumption is explicitly disabled when EKU is negotiated, and resumption secrets are no longer derived.
  - Added conflict resolution rules for simultaneous EKU requests, specifying which party wins and ensuring unaccepted request messages are excluded from transcript hash calculations.
  - Updated DTLS framing logic so that any subsequent application message sent by a responder acts as an implicit ACK if an explicit ACK is lost.
  - Added a deployment considerations section emphasizing explicit opt-in configuration and frequency policies based on time or data volume.

- **Formal Analysis:**
  - Symbolic analysis using the Tamarin prover confirmed that EKU does not regress any core security guarantees of TLS 1.3.
  - Verified secrecy properties under a temporary key compromise with a passive attacker.
  - Proofs for active attacker scenarios and post-handshake authentication are ongoing, targeted for completion by the end of the year.
  - Formal modeling efforts directly contributed to refining the threat model section of the draft.

- **Discussion:**
  - Watson Ladd raised concerns regarding application interface changes and library integration. Yaroslav Rosomakho noted that the deployment considerations section provides guidance on explicit configuration.
  - Muhammad Usama Sardar asked about key storage assumptions in the symbolic model; Felix Linker clarified that the model abstracts storage mechanics and focuses on adversary key access.

